course: dictionary
lesson: 3896
title: Slang and soft swear words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are slang: informal words people use with friends, not in school reports or formal letters. «"Frick" is American slang used instead of the f-word.» So frick is a stand-in, a word people say when they feel annoyed or surprised but do not want to say a much ruder word.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «American slang» tells you where the word mostly comes from, and «used instead of» tells you it replaces another word. Ask yourself: what is the speaker trying to avoid saying? The feeling behind it, such as anger or shock, is the clue to the meaning.
explain: Frick can be a shout, as in «Oh, frick!», or part of a phrase, as in «what the frick», which is a milder version of a shocked exclamation. In slang it can also be used as a verb or an adjective, such as «fricking», but the most important thing to know is that it is a softer swear word.
explain: Even a mild swear word can sound rude to some people, so think about who is listening before you use it. Good readers notice the feeling a word carries, not only its basic meaning.
fact: Slang is informal language that people use in casual talk.
fact: «Frick» is a mild, softer stand-in for a much ruder word.
fact: «Oh, frick!» shows annoyance or surprise.
fact: «What the frick» is a milder version of a rude exclamation of shock.
fact: Frick is mostly used in the US and Canada, and some people still think it sounds rude.
exercise: «"Frick" is American slang used instead of the f-word.» Where is frick mostly used? | *The United States | Wales | Scotland | Australia
exercise: Why do people say frick instead of a ruder word? | To name a sport | *To show annoyance or surprise without using a much ruder word | To ask for a drink | To count to ten
exercise: What does «what the frick» mean? | *A milder version of a rude shout of shock | A thank you for a present | A sneeze | A question about the weather
test: Which word is a softer stand-in for a ruder swear word? | cartoon | apology | hungry | *frick
test: Why might a child avoid saying frick at school? | It is too short to say | *Some people still think it sounds rude | It is a kind of dog | It only means a colour
exam: Which is the best description of frick? | *A mild slang word that stands in for a ruder swear | A polite word for a gift | A number used in maths | A kind of flower
